    {
      "_comment_D": "Layout D \u2014 HWSkin / skinned character meshes (e.g. alicia_final, PlaygroundCompressToonShade_HWSkin). Positions and normals are stored as s16\u00d73 (stride 6). UVs remain f32\u00d72 (stride 8). A bone-weight table of f32 pairs lives at +0x44. The GX display-list pointer is embedded as a non-aligned reloc at an VARIABLE byte offset in the first 0x28 bytes of the descriptor; it must be found by scanning for non-aligned relocs within that window rather than a fixed off_pgx. The unique structural anchor is a self-pointer at desc+0x2c whose resolved value equals desc_base. There is no reliable magic-byte discriminator distinct from Layout C (both use 0x02), so the self-ptr check carries the heaviest score weight.",
